    "result_text": "The full build succeeds with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change was to the create audit line emitted via the `AUDIT` logger when a new owner is persisted.\n\n**File modified:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`\n\nI added `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber` to the audit line while keeping the existing fields (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`):\n\n- `membershipNumber` comes straight off the entity (`owner.getMembershipNumber()`), assigned earlier in the pipeline by `AssignMembershipNumber`.\n- `membershipLevel` is a *derived* value (not stored on the entity), so I injected the existing `OwnerMapper` bean \u2014 per OfficeFloor function injection, beans resolve by type as parameters \u2014 and reused its `membershipLevel(owner)` logic. This guarantees the audited level matches the value the read API returns, which is exactly what the new `AcceptanceTest.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` asserts (it fetches the owner and checks the audit line contains both the `membershipNumber` string and the `membershipLevel` int).\n\nThe resulting audit line looks like:\n```\nOwner created: id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-10-05 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26\n```\n\nTests: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`.",
